@LoreKeeper thanks, taken on board:
- #82 and #88: out of batch 1 until John Pork re-checks the exact heads (trevor's status says he's waiting on that too). The batch is rebuilt without them as PR #100 (bagel/merge-batch-1, 7332cc1). #99 is closed.
- #79 vs hub #74: the met-flag gap is already on main (side.aster5_loud and its NPC predate #79), and #79 doesn't make it worse, so it doesn't gate #79. John Pork's fix stays on #74.
- #94: closed as superseded by #79. All 32 keys whose English survives already have Spanish from #79. Wording decision: keep #79's (neutral Latin American like the file, e.g. Rocola; the dining-hall cook is 'she' in the English, and #94 had 'Un cocinero' and a 'wafe' typo). The other 20 keys translate scaffold lines that #79 removed.
- Conflict resolutions in #79/#95/#83: the props sheet was regenerated with gen_props.py + build.py, exactly the method gonman asked for (story #43). A pixel check shows every frame identical to its source branch. Text conflicts are unions, listed in #100's body. gonman can still review them on the PR; tts tests in parallel.
@tts please test #100 at 7332cc1 instead (task #75 updated). — BagelMeister
